# The mindcraft-webhook Vercel project's dashboard rootDirectory is
# "webhook", so a CLI deploy run from the repo root (the only invocation
# that doesn't hit the CLI's "webhook/webhook does not exist" bug when
# rootDirectory is set) otherwise archives the entire monorepo: 60k+ files,
# a 4.3GB .git history, several 100MB+ image-batch zips at the root, and a
# stray broken symlink in .scratch-pdf-venv/ that fails the archive step
# outright. webhook/ is fully self-contained (own package.json, own
# lockfile, own node_modules), no workspace setup, so everything else here
# is safe to exclude.
#
# Every one of these is anchored with a leading slash (repo root only): an
# unanchored pattern like "data/" matches at ANY depth, and webhook/ has its
# own data/, firebase/, and scripts/ directories the build actually needs
# (webhook/data/*.json in particular, found the hard way when an unanchored
# "data/" here broke the build entirely). node_modules/ is the deliberate
# exception, left unanchored: webhook's own copy should also be excluded,
# Vercel reinstalls it fresh from package-lock.json during its build.
/.git/
/*.zip
/agent_work/
/app/
/data/
/demo-assets/
/docs/
/firebase/
/generated_chapter_images/
/homework/
/img/
/ios-prototype/
/library/
/marketing/
/memory/
/ml/
node_modules/
/pitch/
/scripts/
/sims/
/spark/
/worlds/
/.scratch-pdf-venv/
